#import "/modern-iaf/manuals/layout/manual.typ": *

#idx("Training course, phase 1")#idx("Ground and start-up")Phase 1, Ground and start-up, is the first phase of each jet's course: five #term("lesson")s on the ground at the jet's home base (the Barak at Ramat David, the Sufa at Ramon, the Adir at Nevatim). Each lesson starts cold and dark on the parking spot. The briefing in the game gives the lesson's steps, and the jet's flight manual gives the procedure: the #other("f16i", "cold-start"), the #other("f16d", "cold-start") and the #other("f35i", "cold-start").

#grid-table(
  (auto, 1fr, 1fr),
  ([Lesson], [What it teaches], [How it is graded]),
  [1.1 Cockpit and power], [The cockpit set for the start, the power on and off again, the warning lights, the radio check. No engine.], [Checklist items done; radio calls made.],
  [1.2 Engine start and #term("INS")], [The full start-up by the checklist with the INS aligned, then the shutdown.], [Start-up time to idle with the avionics up; checklist items done; the INS aligned before the taxi.],
  [1.3 Taxi and radio], [The ground calls, the taxi to a runway's #term("holding point") and back, the shutdown.], [Radio calls made; the highest taxi speed; checklist items done.],
  [1.4 At night], [The start-up with the cockpit set for the night, the taxi by night.], [Start-up time; the cockpit lighting set for the night; the highest taxi speed.],
  [1.5 Check ride 1], [Everything of phase 1 alone: start-up, radio, taxi, line-up, taxi back, shutdown.], [Every item of lessons 1.1 to 1.3.],
)

#idx("Check ride 1")Check ride 1 is flown by day, with no instructor's calls and no switch marks; the #term("notebook") is there as always. It has no emergency. A lesson passes when it reaches its end within its time and no item is graded "Unsatisfactory"; the #term("debrief") gives each item's grade (@debrief).
